  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-12-15T05:56:12.998Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Adding a custom repository to the userRepos creates several problems.\n\nWhile they are properly stored in the package cache, they are apparently not being used.\n\nFor what appears to be every other frame, VCC will re-serialize the cache, download the repository and store it in A DIFFERENT CACHE FILE multiple times.\n\nThis results in hundreds of files, with the same content, for the same repository, being created in the cache just from selecting a project in the menu.\n\nNot only does this create a lot of unnecessary files, but it also makes the creator completely unusable, as it takes ages to serialize the cache after just a few seconds of use.\n\nI haven't decompiled the code, *as per ToS*, but I did use dotTrace to profile the application.\n\nIf requested, I can provide a copy of the dump.\n\nBut basically, the biggest problem appears to be the `GetAll` property in `VRC.PackageManagement.Core.Package`, freezing the application for a whole 1:55 minutes, just from selecting a project in the menu.\n\n*EDIT: I've cleared the cache before launching VCC*\n\nDuring the same process, the `CanBeAddedTo` method in `VRC.PackageManagement.Core.Types.Packages.VRCPackageManifest` takes up \"only\" 18 seconds.\n\nI've tried this process with new projects, and ones with VPM packages already installed, and the results are practically the same.\n\nIf further information (or the dotTrace dump) is needed, I'll be happy to provide it.\n\nNot sure how active I'll be on the canny, so you can contact me on Discord at `Fox_score#1678`.",
